```
- This route is protected — it only works if `auth` middleware **calls `next()`** successfully.
- Because of the middleware, `req.username` now holds the username that was inside the JWT token.

```js
let foundUser = null;
for (let i = 0; i < users.length; i++) {
  if (users[i].username === req.username) {
    foundUser = users[i];
  }
}
```
- It searches for the user from your in-memory array using `req.username`.

```js
